nio: halt the init task, not kernel_task, in load_machfile

Runs 613-615 reach exec /sbin/launchd but end at task.c:3126
assert(task != kernel_task).  load_machfile() takes
task = current_task() and, on an exec, calls task_start_halt(task);
the launchd exec runs on the boot thread, so current_task() is
kernel_task and halting it asserts.

XNU reaches load_init_program on the init thread, where current_task()
is the init task.  Reproduce that here: when the exec task is
kernel_task, use proc_find(1)'s task for the halt.  printf confirms it.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/mach_loader.c b/bsd/kern/mach_loader.c
--- a/bsd/kern/mach_loader.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/mach_loader.c
@@ -460,5 +460,14 @@ load_machfile(
 	int in_exec = (imgp->ip_flags & IMGPF_EXEC);
 	task_t task = current_task();
+	/* nio: the init exec runs on the boot thread, so current_task() is
+	 * kernel_task and task_start_halt() would assert.  Use the init task. */
+	if (in_exec && task == kernel_task) {
+		proc_t initp = proc_find(1);
+		if (initp != PROC_NULL) {
+			task = proc_task(initp);
+			printf("nio: machfile: halt init task, not kernel_task\n");
+		}
+	}
 	int64_t                 aslr_page_offset = 0;
 	int64_t                 dyld_aslr_page_offset = 0;
 	int64_t                 aslr_section_size = 0;
